 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508739,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Solve using the quadratic formula: <span data-math=\"{a^2} - 2a-15 = 0\">{a^2} - 2a-15 = 0</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"{a^2} - 2a - 15 = 0\"></span></td>\n<td>The equation is in standard form.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>For the quadratic formula, <span data-math=\"a = 1\"></span>, <span data-math=\"b = -2\"></span>, and <span data-math=\"c = -15\"></span>. Do not get confused because there are two <i>a</i>’s in this exercise.</p>\n<p>The solutions to the equation can be found with the quadratic formula <span data-math=\"\\frac{{ - b \\pm \\sqrt {{b^2} - 4ac} }}{{2a}}\"></span>.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{ - \\left({ - 2} \\right) \\pm \\sqrt {{{\\left({ - 2} \\right)}^2} - 4\\left(1 \\right)\\left({ - 15} \\right)} }}{{2\\left(1 \\right)}}\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n<td>Substitute.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{2 \\pm \\sqrt {4 + 60} }}{2}\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n<td>Simplify.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{2 \\pm \\sqrt {64} }}{2}\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{2 \\pm 8}}{2}\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"a = \\frac{{2 + 8}}{2}\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"a = \\frac{{2 - 8}}{2}\"></span></td>\n<td>Rewrite to show two solutions.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"a = \\frac{{10}}{2}\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"a = \\frac{{ - 6}}{2}\"></span></td>\n<td>Simplify.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"a = 5\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"a = - 3\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Checking is left for you.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"a = 5\">a = 5</span>, <span data-math=\"a = - 3\">a = - 3</span>"
    }
   ],
